bdscrub: sources of the reference data
======================================

The code of bdscrub is licensed under the MIT licence (see LICENSE).
The package also contains reference data compiled from public sources.
Only names, codes and their relations (facts) were taken from them.

1. Post offices and post codes (data set bd_postcodes)
   Source: Bangladesh Post, district post code pages of the Postmaster
   General offices, https://bdpost.gov.bd, read October 2026.
   The list is published openly by Bangladesh Post on its public website.
   Two post office names with typing errors on the source pages were
   corrected; the corrections are recorded in the `note` column.

2. Boundary-file names and place codes of thanas and districts
   (columns map_name and pcode of bd_thanas, district_map of bd_districts)
   Source: administrative boundaries of the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics
   (BBS) as distributed on the Humanitarian Data Exchange (HDX), taken from
   the CRAN package 'bangladesh' (Hossain, 2022).
   Licence: as stated on the HDX dataset page (to be confirmed and named
   here before the CRAN submission).

3. List of thanas (rural thanas = upazilas)
   Checked against "Upazilas of Bangladesh", Wikipedia,
   https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upazilas_of_Bangladesh (CC BY-SA 4.0),
   read October 2026. Only place names were used; no text was copied.

4. District and division names and codes (bd_districts, bd_divisions)
   ISO 3166-2:BD (including the 2018 spelling changes) and the geographic
   codes of the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics.

5. Mobile prefixes (bd_phone_prefixes)
   Prefix allocations of the Bangladesh Telecommunication Regulatory
   Commission (BTRC).

Spelling variants of place names were collected by the authors from survey
and administrative data.
